consensus_answer:
B9.322 ... Claiming WA is voluntary [EXC: 9.323], and can be done by a unit at five times: 
- during its setup; 
- at the end of any RPh (step 1.32B of ASOP, ATTACKER first); 
- during its MPh/APh (either as part of, or before/after MF/MP expenditures); 
- when losing HIP status; 
- whenever all enemy units lose/forfeit WA over shared wall/hedge hexsides.

During the enemy MPh is not one of those five times, so your squad in a building cannot claim WA when an Enemy unit moves adjacent.
It could have anticipated that during the preceding RPh.
During the enemy MPh *can* be one of the times if an enemy unit drops WA. If an enemy unit is already adjacent and has WA but it moves to another adjacent hex across a wall hexside, the moving unit drops WA for a moment [B9.41]. The DEFENDER can steal WA at this time. 

It can also happen if an enemy unit leaves a friendly unit's location. While friendly and enemy units are in the same location neither can claim WA. As soon as the enemy unit leaves the friendly unit can (or must in the case of mandatory WA) claim WA.

