replies.body:
The Tome says: 10.531 OPEN GROUND: For purposes of rout determination, Dash, concealment gain/loss, and Interdiction, an Open Ground hex is any hex in which any Interdictor could apply, during a hypothetical Defensive First Fire opportunity (regardless of what attacks it actually made in previous phases), the -1 FFMO DRM.

So, if a German squad in APh advance in CC with a Russian squad and then a concealed German HS advance in a road, in LOS with the Russian squad and no Hindrance... would the HS lose the Concealment?

- the Russian squad is still in Good Order;
- the German HS is in LOS with no TEM or Hindrance to protect them;
- the Russian squad can't Defensive First Fire out of his HEX due to CC (7.212 TARGET SELECTION LIMITS);

In my understanding, the HS should remain Concealed... but several seasoned player say the opposite. 
And this "hypothetical" statement drives me crazy :soblue:

The orchard is the clue;

FFMO applies to movement in the open and is not directly related to whether a TEM is applied or not to a specific attack.

Any hex that may have TEM is considered non-open ground for FFMO, regardless if you actually apply the TEM to the current attack or not.

